response:
**Gates before launch.** I run these in order and stop at the first one that fails. First, I confirm that `spe/predictions/r04.yaml` and `spe/plans/r04.md` are committed and unchanged since that commit. Gate 1 is the grader selftest. I turn `spe/evals/tasks/answers.json` into trial output and run `spe/evals/graders/grade.py` on it, and every row must pass on both `label.category` and `label.priority`. An empty result and a result with every label deliberately wrong must both fail. Gate 2 is the control. I regrade round 3's saved trial outputs with this round's `grade.py`, and the numbers must equal the round 3 measured values in `spe/prediction-log.md`. Any difference is a grader change. In that case I log it in `spe/failures.md` with both numbers side by side and stop before launch. Gate 3 is the dry run. I launch the script with `{"only": ["B:T001", "C2:T001", "C2:T017"], "trialsPerCell": 2, "capUsd": 2}`. It passes only if every trial completes and reports `cost_usd`, the runner accepts `C2`, clean transcripts produce no leak-scan matches, every completed trial gets a grader row, and the judge returns a score for every reply. The dry run also confirms the runner, grader and ticket-path formats that the script assumes. When all three gates pass, I save the script as `spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js`, commit it locally, and launch it with `{"capUsd": 40}`. The Workflow returns at launch, and I close out the round when its completion notice arrives.

```js
export const meta = {
  name: 'triage-spe-eval',
  description: 'SPE eval for the triage agent. Configs B and C2, 50 tickets, 5 trials per cell. Code grader first, blind Opus tone judge second, capped top-up on split cells, then failure analysis and a completeness critic. Spend and agent count are capped in args.',
  phases: ['Trials', 'Leak scan', 'Grade', 'Judge', 'Top-up', 'Synthesis'],
};

// Defaults below are arguments. If the dry run shows a mismatch, fix it in args, not in code.
// runnerCmd: the ticket runner from last round. It must accept config C2, write result.json and
//   transcript.jsonl into {out}, and print the result JSON on its last line.
// graderCmd: grade.py with --answers, --results, --ticket and --json. It prints one row per trial.
// tickets: T001 to T050 unless args.tickets is given.
// estTrialUsd and estJudgeUsd come from the plan's unmeasured estimate. Each trial's reported
//   cost_usd replaces the estimate when it arrives. Judge calls are charged at the estimate.
// The spend cap covers triage API calls and judge calls. maxAgents caps the Workflow's own agents.

const ROUND = 4;
const RR = String(ROUND).padStart(2, '0');
const A = (typeof args === 'object' && args !== null) ? args : {};

const EXPECTED_TICKETS = 50;
const TRIALS = A.trialsPerCell ?? 5;
const TICKETS = A.tickets ?? Array.from({ length: EXPECTED_TICKETS }, (_, i) => `T${String(i + 1).padStart(3, '0')}`);
const ONLY = Array.isArray(A.only) ? A.only : null;
const CAP_USD = A.capUsd ?? 40;
const EST_TRIAL_USD = A.estTrialUsd ?? 0.05;
const EST_JUDGE_USD = A.estJudgeUsd ?? 0.15;
const MAX_AGENTS = A.maxAgents ?? 300;
const TOPUP_PER_CELL = A.topUpPerCell ?? 5;
const TOPUP_MAX_TRIALS = A.topUpMaxTrials ?? 100;
const WAVE = A.concurrency ?? 10;
const OUT = A.outDir ?? `spe/runs/r${RR}`;
const RUNNER_CMD = A.runnerCmd ?? 'node spe/evals/harness/run-ticket.js --config {config} --ticket {ticket} --trial {trial} --out {out}';
const GRADER_CMD = A.graderCmd ?? 'python3 spe/evals/graders/grade.py --answers spe/evals/tasks/answers.json --results {dir} --ticket {ticket} --json';
const TICKET_PATH = A.ticketPath ?? 'spe/evals/tasks/tickets/{ticket}.json';
const JUDGE_RUBRIC = 'spe/evals/graders/judge.md';

// A trial transcript that names any of these paths counts as a peek, and the trial is voided.
const LEAK_PATTERN = 'answers\\.json|grade\\.py|judge\\.md|spe/evals/graders|spe/predictions|spe/plans';
const CMD_PATTERN = new RegExp(`${LEAK_PATTERN}|spe/evals/tasks`);

const CONFIGS = [
  { id: 'B', model: 'claude-sonnet-5-5', prompt: '12-line', tools: '6 tools', role: 'reference, same as last round' },
  { id: 'C2', model: 'claude-sonnet-5-5', prompt: '12-line', tools: '3 merged tools plus a separate check_status tool', role: 'changes only the tool set' },
];

// ---------- schemas ----------

const CELL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['trials', 'commands_run'],
  properties: {
    commands_run: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    trials: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['trial', 'status'],
        properties: {
          trial: { type: 'integer' },
          status: { enum: ['completed', 'rate_limited', 'harness_error'] },
          category: { type: ['string', 'null'] },   // no enum on purpose: grade.py must see raw labels
          priority: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
          reply: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
          input_tokens: { type: ['number', 'null'] },
          output_tokens: { type: ['number', 'null'] },
          tool_calls: { type: ['number', 'null'] },
          tool_errors: { type: ['number', 'null'] },
          runtime_ms: { type: ['number', 'null'] },
          cost_usd: { type: ['number', 'null'] },
          transcript_path: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
          error: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};

const SCAN_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['ok', 'matched'],
  properties: {
    ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    matched: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    error: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
  },
};

const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['grader_ok', 'rows'],
  properties: {
    grader_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    grader_error: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
    rows: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['config', 'ticket', 'trial', 'category_ok', 'priority_ok'],
        properties: {
          config: { type: 'string' },
          ticket: { type: 'string' },
          trial: { type: 'integer' },
          category_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
          priority_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
          expected_category: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
          expected_priority: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};

const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['scores'],
  properties: {
    scores: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['rid', 'score', 'pass', 'reason'],
        properties: {
          rid: { type: 'string' },
          score: { type: 'number' },
          pass: { type: 'boolean' },
          reason: { type: 'string' },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};

const FA_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['failure_types', 'harness_issues', 'suspect_labels'],
  properties: {
    failure_types: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['name', 'kind', 'existing_f', 'what', 'how_to_spot', 'seen_in', 'count_by_config', 'fix'],
        properties: {
          name: { type: 'string' },
          kind: { enum: ['model', 'prompt', 'tool', 'grader', 'harness'] },
          existing_f: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
          what: { type: 'string' },
          how_to_spot: { type: 'string' },
          seen_in: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
          count_by_config: { type: 'object' },
          fix: { type: 'string' },
        },
      },
    },
    harness_issues: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    suspect_labels: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
};

const CRITIC_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['scorable', 'gaps'],
  properties: {
    scorable: { type: 'boolean' },
    gaps: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['item', 'detail', 'severity'],
        properties: {
          item: { type: 'string' },
          detail: { type: 'string' },
          severity: { enum: ['blocker', 'minor'] },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};

// ---------- helpers ----------

const state = { spent: 0, judgeUsd: 0, reserved: 0, agents: 0, capHit: false, skips: [], halt: null };
const rows = [];

const range = (a, b) => Array.from({ length: Math.max(0, b - a + 1) }, (_, i) => a + i);
const fill = (tpl, vals) => tpl.replace(/\{(\w+)\}/g, (_, k) => String(vals[k]));
const uniqueTickets = (rs) => [...new Set(rs.map((r) => r.ticket))];
const mean = (xs) => (xs.length ? xs.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / xs.length : null);
const num = (x) => (typeof x === 'number' ? x : null);
const halt = (why) => { if (!state.halt) { state.halt = why; log(`HALT: ${why}`); } };
const voidRow = (r, why) => { if (!r.voided) { r.voided = true; r.voidWhy = why; } };

function takeAgent(what) {
  if (state.agents >= MAX_AGENTS) {
    state.skips.push({ what, why: 'agent cap' });
    log(`Skipped ${what}: agent cap ${MAX_AGENTS} reached.`);
    return false;
  }
  state.agents += 1;
  return true;
}

async function safeAgent(prompt, opts) {
  try { return await agent(prompt, opts); } catch (e) { log(`${opts.label} failed: ${e}`); return null; }
}

async function inWaves(thunks) {
  const out = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < thunks.length; i += WAVE) out.push(...(await parallel(thunks.slice(i, i + WAVE))));
  return out;
}

function rng(seed) {
  let s = seed >>> 0;
  return () => {
    s = (s + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;
    let t = s;
    t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);
    t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);
    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;
  };
}

function shuffled(xs, seed) {
  const r = rng(seed);
  const a = xs.slice();
  for (let i = a.length - 1; i > 0; i--) { const j = Math.floor(r() * (i + 1)); [a[i], a[j]] = [a[j], a[i]]; }
  return a;
}

// ---------- trials ----------

function trialPrompt(cmds) {
  return [
    'You run trials of a support-ticket triage agent for an eval. Your only job is to run the commands below and copy what they print.',
    '',
    'Commands, one per trial, in order:',
    ...cmds.map((c, i) => `${i + 1}. ${c}`),
    '',
    'Each command prints one JSON object on its last line. For each trial, copy: trial, category and priority from label, reply, input_tokens, output_tokens, tool_calls, tool_errors, runtime_ms, cost_usd, transcript_path, error.',
    '',
    'Rules:',
    '- Run only the commands listed. Do not open, list, search, or print any file or directory. Running the commands is allowed.',
    '- Copy values exactly as printed. Do not correct, normalize, or judge a label or a reply.',
    '- Set status to "completed" when the command printed a result. Set "rate_limited" for a rate-limit error. Set "harness_error" for any other failure.',
    '- Retry a failed trial once before you report it.',
    '- In commands_run, list every shell command you ran, exactly as you typed it.',
  ].join('\n');
}

async function runCell(cfg, ticket, trialNums, phaseName) {
  const key = `${cfg.id}:${ticket}`;
  if (state.capHit) {
    state.skips.push({ what: `${phaseName} ${key}`, trials: trialNums, why: 'spend cap' });
    return [];
  }
  // Reserve synchronously before the first await, so parallel thunks cannot overrun the cap.
  let n = 0;
  while (n < trialNums.length && state.spent + state.reserved + (n + 1) * EST_TRIAL_USD <= CAP_USD) n += 1;
  const run = trialNums.slice(0, n);
  const skipped = trialNums.slice(n);
  if (skipped.length) {
    state.capHit = true;
    state.skips.push({ what: `${phaseName} ${key}`, trials: skipped, why: 'spend cap' });
    log(`Skipped ${key} trials ${skipped.join(', ')}: they would cross the $${CAP_USD} cap.`);
  }
  if (!run.length) return [];
  if (!takeAgent(`${phaseName} ${key}`)) return [];
  const held = run.length * EST_TRIAL_USD;
  state.reserved += held;

  const cmds = run.map((k) => fill(RUNNER_CMD, { config: cfg.id, ticket, trial: k, out: `${OUT}/${cfg.id}/${ticket}/t${k}` }));
  let res = null;
  try {
    res = await agent(trialPrompt(cmds), { label: `${phaseName.toLowerCase()} ${key}`, phase: phaseName, schema: CELL_SCHEMA });
  } catch (e) {
    res = { commands_run: [], trials: run.map((k) => ({ trial: k, status: 'harness_error', error: String(e) })) };
  }
  state.reserved -= held;

  const badCmd = (res.commands_run || []).some((c) => CMD_PATTERN.test(c));
  return run.map((k, i) => {
    const t = (res.trials || []).find((x) => x.trial === k) || (res.trials || [])[i] || { status: 'harness_error', error: 'missing from agent report' };
    const cost = num(t.cost_usd) ?? EST_TRIAL_USD; // charge the estimate when cost is unknown
    state.spent += cost;
    return {
      key, config: cfg.id, ticket, trial: k, topup: phaseName === 'Top-up',
      status: t.status, category: t.category ?? null, priority: t.priority ?? null, reply: t.reply ?? null,
      input_tokens: num(t.input_tokens), output_tokens: num(t.output_tokens), tool_calls: num(t.tool_calls),
      tool_errors: num(t.tool_errors), runtime_ms: num(t.runtime_ms), cost_usd: cost, cost_measured: num(t.cost_usd) !== null,
      transcript_path: t.transcript_path ?? null, error: t.error ?? null,
      badCmd, voided: false, voidWhy: null, graded: false,
    };
  });
}

// ---------- leak scan ----------

async function leakScan(phaseName) {
  for (const r of rows) {
    if (r.status !== 'completed' || r.voided) continue;
    if (r.badCmd) voidRow(r, 'peek: a command touched a protected path');
    else if (!r.transcript_path) voidRow(r, 'no transcript to scan');
  }
  if (!takeAgent(`${phaseName} leak scan`)) { halt('leak scan could not run: agent cap'); return; }
  const cmd = `grep -rlE --include='transcript*' '${LEAK_PATTERN}' ${OUT}`;
  const s = await safeAgent([
    'You scan eval transcripts for reads of protected files. Run this command exactly once:',
    '',
    cmd,
    '',
    'Put every file path it prints into matched. Exit code 1 with no output means no matches. That is a success, so set ok to true and leave matched empty.',
    'Set ok to false and copy the error if the command fails in any other way. Do not open the matched files. Do not edit anything.',
  ].join('\n'), { label: `${phaseName.toLowerCase()} leak scan`, phase: phaseName, schema: SCAN_SCHEMA });
  if (!s || !s.ok) { halt(`leak scan failed: ${s ? s.error : 'agent error'}`); return; }

  for (const r of rows) {
    if (r.status !== 'completed' || r.voided) continue;
    if (s.matched.some((p) => p.includes(`/${r.config}/${r.ticket}/t${r.trial}/`))) voidRow(r, 'peek: transcript names a protected path');
  }
  const peeks = rows.filter((r) => (r.voidWhy || '').startsWith('peek'));
  const noTranscript = rows.filter((r) => r.voidWhy === 'no transcript to scan');
  if (noTranscript.length) log(`Voided ${noTranscript.length} trial(s) with no transcript to scan.`);
  if (peeks.length) halt(`answer key exposure: ${peeks.length} trial(s) voided, e.g. ${peeks.slice(0, 3).map((r) => `${r.key} t${r.trial}`).join(', ')}`);
}

// ---------- code grader ----------

async function gradeTicket(ticket, phaseName) {
  if (!takeAgent(`grade ${ticket}`)) return { ticket, ok: false, error: 'agent cap', rows: [] };
  const cmd = fill(GRADER_CMD, { dir: OUT, ticket });
  const g = await safeAgent([
    'You run the code grader for an eval. Run this command exactly once and copy its output into the schema:',
    '',
    cmd,
    '',
    'Do not edit, create, or delete any file. Do not grade anything yourself.',
    'Copy one row per graded trial with config, ticket, trial, category_ok, priority_ok, expected_category, and expected_priority.',
    'Set grader_ok to false and copy the error text if the command exits non-zero or prints output you cannot parse.',
  ].join('\n'), { label: `grade ${ticket}`, phase: phaseName, schema: GRADE_SCHEMA });
  if (!g) return { ticket, ok: false, error: 'agent error', rows: [] };
  return { ticket, ok: !!g.grader_ok, error: g.grader_error || null, rows: g.rows || [] };
}

async function gradeRows(filter, phaseName) {
  const todo = rows.filter((r) => filter(r) && r.status === 'completed' && !r.voided && !r.graded);
  const results = await inWaves(uniqueTickets(todo).map((t) => () => gradeTicket(t, phaseName)));
  for (const g of results) if (!g.ok) halt(`grader failed on ${g.ticket}: ${g.error}`);
  const missing = [];
  for (const r of todo) {
    const g = results.find((x) => x.ticket === r.ticket)?.rows.find((x) => x.config === r.config && x.trial === r.trial);
    if (!g) { missing.push(`${r.key} t${r.trial}`); continue; }
    Object.assign(r, {
      graded: true,
      category_ok: g.category_ok,
      priority_ok: g.priority_ok,
      label_ok: g.category_ok && g.priority_ok,
      expected_category: g.expected_category ?? null,
      expected_priority: g.expected_priority ?? null,
    });
  }
  if (missing.length) halt(`grader returned no row for ${missing.length} completed trial(s), e.g. ${missing.slice(0, 3).join(', ')}`);
}

// ---------- tone judge (blind, Opus) ----------

async function judgeTicket(ticket, idx) {
  const items = rows.filter((r) => r.ticket === ticket && !r.topup && r.graded && typeof r.reply === 'string');
  if (!items.length) return;
  if (state.capHit || state.spent + state.reserved + EST_JUDGE_USD > CAP_USD) {
    state.capHit = true;
    state.skips.push({ what: `judge ${ticket}`, why: 'spend cap' });
    log(`Skipped judge for ${ticket}: it would cross the $${CAP_USD} cap.`);
    return;
  }
  if (!takeAgent(`judge ${ticket}`)) return;
  state.reserved += EST_JUDGE_USD;

  const blind = shuffled(items, ROUND * 1000 + idx).map((r, i) => ({ rid: `R${i + 1}`, row: r }));
  const j = await safeAgent([
    'You are the tone judge for drafted first replies to one support ticket.',
    `Read the rubric at ${JUDGE_RUBRIC} and apply it exactly. Read the ticket at ${fill(TICKET_PATH, { ticket })}.`,
    'Do not open any other file. Do not open answers.json, anything under spe/predictions/, or anything under spe/plans/.',
    'You do not know which system wrote each reply. Several replies may come from the same system. Score each reply on its own.',
    'Judge tone only, as the rubric defines it. Do not score the category or the priority.',
    'Return one score per reply id, with pass, and a one-sentence reason.',
    '',
    ...blind.map((b) => `--- ${b.rid} ---\n${b.row.reply}`),
  ].join('\n'), { label: `judge ${ticket}`, phase: 'Judge', schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: 'opus' });

  state.reserved -= EST_JUDGE_USD;
  state.spent += EST_JUDGE_USD;
  state.judgeUsd += EST_JUDGE_USD;
  if (!j) return;
  for (const b of blind) {
    const s = j.scores.find((x) => x.rid === b.rid);
    if (s) Object.assign(b.row, { tone_score: s.score, tone_pass: s.pass, tone_reason: s.reason });
  }
}

// ---------- summary ----------

function configMetrics(cfgId, withTopup) {
  const all = rows.filter((r) => r.config === cfgId && (withTopup || !r.topup));
  const done = all.filter((r) => r.graded);
  const judged = done.filter((r) => !r.topup && typeof r.tone_score === 'number');
  const pick = (f) => done.map(f).filter((x) => typeof x === 'number');
  return {
    n_trials_run: all.length,
    n_completed_graded: done.length,
    n_rate_limited: all.filter((r) => r.status === 'rate_limited').length,
    n_harness_error: all.filter((r) => r.status === 'harness_error').length,
    n_voided: all.filter((r) => r.voided).length,
    category_accuracy: { value: mean(done.map((r) => (r.category_ok ? 1 : 0))), check: 'grade.py: label.category vs answers.json' },
    priority_accuracy: { value: mean(done.map((r) => (r.priority_ok ? 1 : 0))), check: 'grade.py: label.priority vs answers.json' },
    label_accuracy: { value: mean(done.map((r) => (r.label_ok ? 1 : 0))), check: 'grade.py: category and priority both match' },
    tone_mean: { value: withTopup ? null : mean(judged.map((r) => r.tone_score)), n: judged.length, check: 'Opus judge with judge.md' },
    tone_pass_rate: { value: withTopup ? null : mean(judged.map((r) => (r.tone_pass ? 1 : 0))), n: judged.length, check: 'Opus judge with judge.md' },
    runtime_ms_mean: mean(pick((r) => r.runtime_ms)),
    tool_calls_mean: mean(pick((r) => r.tool_calls)),
    tokens_mean: mean(pick((r) => (num(r.input_tokens) ?? 0) + (num(r.output_tokens) ?? 0))),
    tool_errors_mean: mean(pick((r) => r.tool_errors)),
    trials_with_tool_errors: done.filter((r) => (r.tool_errors ?? 0) > 0).length,
    cost_usd: all.reduce((a, r) => a + r.cost_usd, 0),
  };
}

function buildSummary(cells) {
  const metrics = {};
  for (const c of CONFIGS) metrics[c.id] = { base: configMetrics(c.id, false), with_topup: configMetrics(c.id, true) };
  return {
    round: ROUND,
    mode: ONLY ? 'dry run' : 'full',
    configs: CONFIGS,
    trials_per_cell: TRIALS,
    tickets: ONLY ? uniqueTickets(cells) : TICKETS.length,
    note: 'Base metrics use only the planned trials per cell and are the numbers to score against the prediction. with_topup adds the extra trials on split cells.',
    metrics,
    cells: cells.map((c) => {
      const b = rows.filter((r) => r.key === c.key && !r.topup && r.graded);
      const t = rows.filter((r) => r.key === c.key && r.topup && r.graded);
      return { key: c.key, base_graded: b.length, base_label_pass: b.filter((r) => r.label_ok).length, topup_graded: t.length, topup_label_pass: t.filter((r) => r.label_ok).length };
    }),
    spend: {
      cap_usd: CAP_USD,
      spent_usd: state.spent,
      trial_usd_measured: rows.filter((r) => r.cost_measured).reduce((a, r) => a + r.cost_usd, 0),
      trial_usd_estimated: rows.filter((r) => !r.cost_measured).reduce((a, r) => a + r.cost_usd, 0),
      judge_usd_estimated: state.judgeUsd,
      cap_hit: state.capHit,
    },
    agents_used: state.agents,
    agent_cap: MAX_AGENTS,
    skips: state.skips,
    voided: rows.filter((r) => r.voided).map((r) => ({ cell: r.key, trial: r.trial, why: r.voidWhy })),
    harness_errors: rows.filter((r) => r.status !== 'completed').map((r) => ({ cell: r.key, trial: r.trial, status: r.status, error: r.error })),
    judge_note: 'The tone judge is Opus, the same model family as the triage agent. No other-family judge was available.',
    halt: state.halt || (state.capHit ? 'spend cap reached. Skipped work is listed in skips.' : null),
  };
}

// ---------- main ----------

async function main() {
  const allCells = [];
  for (const cfg of CONFIGS) for (const ticket of TICKETS) allCells.push({ cfg, ticket, key: `${cfg.id}:${ticket}` });
  if (!ONLY && TICKETS.length !== EXPECTED_TICKETS) {
    throw new Error(`Expected ${EXPECTED_TICKETS} tickets, got ${TICKETS.length}. The approved plan fixes the task set.`);
  }
  const unknown = ONLY ? ONLY.filter((k) => !allCells.some((c) => c.key === k)) : [];
  if (unknown.length) throw new Error(`args.only names unknown cells: ${unknown.join(', ')}`);
  const cells = ONLY ? allCells.filter((c) => ONLY.includes(c.key)) : allCells;

  log(`Round ${ROUND}: ${cells.length} cells x ${TRIALS} trials. Spend cap $${CAP_USD}. Agent cap ${MAX_AGENTS}. Output ${OUT}.`);
  log('The tone judge is Opus, the same model family as the triage agent. No judge from another family is available here, so shared blind spots are possible.');

  phase('Trials');
  rows.push(...(await inWaves(cells.map((c) => () => runCell(c.cfg, c.ticket, range(1, TRIALS), 'Trials')))).flat());
  log(`Trials: ${rows.filter((r) => r.status === 'completed').length} completed of ${rows.length} run.`);

  phase('Leak scan');
  await leakScan('Leak scan');
  if (state.halt) return buildSummary(cells);

  phase('Grade');
  await gradeRows((r) => !r.topup, 'Grade');
  if (state.halt) return buildSummary(cells);

  phase('Judge');
  const judgeList = uniqueTickets(rows.filter((r) => !r.topup && r.graded));
  await inWaves(judgeList.map((t, i) => () => judgeTicket(t, i)));

  phase('Top-up');
  if (state.capHit) {
    log('Top-up skipped: the spend cap was reached.');
  } else {
    const split = cells.filter((c) => {
      const g = rows.filter((r) => r.key === c.key && !r.topup && r.graded);
      const p = g.filter((r) => r.label_ok).length;
      return g.length > 0 && p > 0 && p < g.length;
    });
    let left = TOPUP_MAX_TRIALS;
    const plan = [];
    for (const c of split) {
      const n = Math.min(TOPUP_PER_CELL, left);
      if (n <= 0) { state.skips.push({ what: `top-up ${c.key}`, why: 'top-up cap' }); continue; }
      left -= n;
      plan.push({ c, nums: range(TRIALS + 1, TRIALS + n) });
    }
    log(`Top-up: ${split.length} split cell(s), ${plan.length} scheduled, ${TOPUP_MAX_TRIALS - left} extra trial(s). Top-up trials are graded but not judged.`);
    const extra = (await inWaves(plan.map((p) => () => runCell(p.c.cfg, p.c.ticket, p.nums, 'Top-up')))).flat();
    rows.push(...extra);
    if (extra.length) {
      await leakScan('Top-up');
      if (!state.halt) await gradeRows((r) => r.topup, 'Top-up');
    }
    if (state.halt) return buildSummary(cells);
  }

  phase('Synthesis');
  const summary = buildSummary(cells);
  const misses = rows.filter((r) => r.graded && !r.label_ok).map((r) => ({
    cell: r.key, trial: r.trial, topup: r.topup,
    got: { category: r.category, priority: r.priority },
    expected: { category: r.expected_category, priority: r.expected_priority },
    reply_start: (r.reply || '').slice(0, 400),
  }));
  const toneFails = rows.filter((r) => r.tone_pass === false).map((r) => ({ cell: r.key, trial: r.trial, reason: r.tone_reason }));
  const cfgText = CONFIGS.map((c) => `${c.id}: ${c.model}, ${c.prompt} prompt, ${c.tools} (${c.role})`).join('\n');

  const fa = takeAgent('failure analysis') ? await safeAgent([
    'You analyze failures from an eval of a support-ticket triage agent. Two configurations ran the same tickets:',
    cfgText,
    '',
    'Read spe/failures.md to see the failure types already numbered. Do not read spe/predictions/ or spe/plans/, so that what was expected does not shape your analysis. Do not write or edit any file.',
    'A label miss is a trial where the category or the priority did not match the reference label. Tone failures come from the judge. Harness errors and rate limits are not model failures. List them under harness_issues.',
    'Group the misses into failure types. For each type, give the name, kind, the existing F number if it matches one or null, what happened, how to spot it, the cells and trials where it was seen, the count per config, and a proposed fix.',
    'In suspect_labels, name any cell where the reference label itself looks wrong or the ticket is ambiguous. The support lead decides those.',
    '',
    `Label misses: ${JSON.stringify(misses)}`,
    `Tone failures: ${JSON.stringify(toneFails)}`,
    `Harness errors: ${JSON.stringify(summary.harness_errors)}`,
    `Voided trials: ${JSON.stringify(summary.voided)}`,
  ].join('\n'), { label: 'failure analysis', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: FA_SCHEMA, model: 'opus' }) : null;

  const critic = takeAgent('completeness critic') ? await safeAgent([
    'You check an eval run for completeness before anyone reads its numbers. Do not read spe/predictions/ or spe/plans/. Do not write or edit any file.',
    'Check each item below and report every gap with its severity:',
    `1. Every cell in scope has ${TRIALS} completed and graded base trials, or each missing trial has a logged reason (skip, harness error, or void).`,
    '2. Every graded base trial has a tone score, or its judge call is listed in skips.',
    '3. Every skip names the cap that caused it.',
    '4. Voided trials and harness errors are left out of the accuracy denominators.',
    '5. Each trial records runtime, tool calls, tokens, tool errors, and cost.',
    '6. Top-up trials are reported apart from the base metrics.',
    '7. Spend stayed under the cap. Estimated and measured spend are shown apart.',
    '8. The failure analysis covers every label miss and keeps harness issues apart from model failures.',
    'Set scorable to true only if the base metrics are complete enough to compare against a prediction.',
    '',
    `Summary: ${JSON.stringify(summary)}`,
    `Failure analysis: ${JSON.stringify(fa)}`,
    `Label misses: ${misses.length}`,
  ].join('\n'), { label: 'completeness critic', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: CRITIC_SCHEMA, model: 'opus' }) : null;

  return { ...summary, failure_analysis: fa, critic };
}

// Same return convention as r03-workflow.js.
return await main();
